\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Long-horizon Dysts forecasting. Each cell is the cross-system IQM of the per-system IQM-over-seeds (system standard deviation in parentheses), followed by $[K/15]$ -- per-system one-sided paired Wilcoxon vs the Dense MLP baseline, Holm-corrected across the $15$ systems at $\alpha {=}0.05$. At $n_{\rm  seed}{=}10$ the exact paired-Wilcoxon $p$-floor is $1/2^{10}{\approx }10^{-3}$, just below Holm's per-system threshold $\alpha /15{\approx }3{\times }10^{-3}$, but residual seed dispersion holds K to $0$--$1$ in most cells; a one-sided binomial sign test on the per-system IQM of $\log _{10}$-MSE deltas is reported in the body text and is the more sensitive within-system stat at this design. LISTA-D: dense-transition LISTA. LISTA-BD: block-diagonal LISTA at $\lambda _{\rm  sp}\in \{3{\times }10^{-3},6{\times }10^{-3}\}$. Sparse/Sparse MLP, BD/Dense MLP: matched standard-sampling MLP roots. Cross-system $\log _{10}$ standard deviation in \cref  {app:dysts_full}.}}{19}{table.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:dysts_long}{{4}{19}{Long-horizon Dysts forecasting. Each cell is the cross-system IQM of the per-system IQM-over-seeds (system standard deviation in parentheses), followed by $[K/15]$ -- per-system one-sided paired Wilcoxon vs the Dense MLP baseline, Holm-corrected across the $15$ systems at $\alpha {=}0.05$. At $n_{\rm seed}{=}10$ the exact paired-Wilcoxon $p$-floor is $1/2^{10}{\approx }10^{-3}$, just below Holm's per-system threshold $\alpha /15{\approx }3{\times }10^{-3}$, but residual seed dispersion holds K to $0$--$1$ in most cells; a one-sided binomial sign test on the per-system IQM of $\log _{10}$-MSE deltas is reported in the body text and is the more sensitive within-system stat at this design. LISTA-D: dense-transition LISTA. LISTA-BD: block-diagonal LISTA at $\lambda _{\rm sp}\in \{3{\times }10^{-3},6{\times }10^{-3}\}$. Sparse/Sparse MLP, BD/Dense MLP: matched standard-sampling MLP roots. Cross-system $\log _{10}$ standard deviation in \cref {app:dysts_full}}{table.caption.24}{}}
\newlabel{tab:dysts_long@cref}{{[table][4][]4}{[1][17][]19}{}{}{}}
